{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KDq5eomT4yXU5N3J5eSDbP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-byO20i/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e29688-e74b-4241-a01a-4b7b8c9dd3e3","uuid":"2fde706b-0c65-4f4f-9dcf-d2a20152dcd5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:12:30.664Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-byO20i/README.md","oldString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Prompt caching is on: the first system\nblock (coaching rules + athlete profile) carries a `cache_control` marker so the\ntool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read it from\ncache. Facts and today's date are in a second, uncached system block, so a\n`save_fact` write does not evict the cached instructions.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":8,"lines":[" Run it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type"," messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).","-Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the first system","+block (coaching rules + athlete profile) carries a `cache_control` marker so the","+tool-loop rounds and follow-up messages inside the 5-minute window read it from","+cache. Facts and today's date are in a second, uncached system block, so a","+`save_fact` write does not evict the cached instructions."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KDq5eomT4yXU5N3J5eSDbP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS6ARCJe9dWU1mSmuxjj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JYEAedkjBgMyBmfymuh2vh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-byO20i/ANSWER.md","content":"# Answer: save_fact evicts the cached system prompt\n\n## Cause\n\n`build_system()` put the whole system prompt into one text block and marked it\n`cache_control: ephemeral`. That block contained:\n\n1. the static coaching rules (`INSTRUCTIONS`),\n2. the athlete profile (name, zones, goal, language), which is stable,\n3. the long-term facts, which `save_fact` appends to, and\n4. today's date, which changes daily.\n\nPrompt caching matches the prefix in order (tools, then system, then messages).\nSince the facts were inside the cached block, any `save_fact` changed the block,\nso the next call missed the cache and paid cache-creation for the whole prefix.\nThat matches `logs/usage.jsonl` and `NOTES.md`: the call after each save shows\n`cache_read_input_tokens: 0` and a fresh `cache_creation_input_tokens`.\n\n## Change (`bot.py`)\n\n- `athlete_profile(a)`: name, sport, zones, goal, language. Stable across `save_fact`.\n- `athlete_facts(a, today)`: today's date and the facts list. Volatile.\n- `build_system()` now returns two text blocks:\n  - block 0: `INSTRUCTIONS` + profile, with `cache_control: ephemeral`\n  - block 1: facts and date, no cache marker\n\nA `save_fact` now changes only block 1, which is after the breakpoint, so block 0\nstill reads from cache. The tool list and messages are untouched.\n\n`README.md` is updated to describe the two blocks.\n\n## Verification\n\nChecked locally without calling the API (no key used, `data/athletes.json` not\nwritten):\n\n- block 0 is byte-identical before and after appending a fact in memory;\n- block 1 changes as expected;\n- only block 0 carries `cache_control`;\n- tools and the request shape are unchanged.\n\n## Open risk: cache minimum\n\nSonnet only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens. My rough estimate for\nblock 0 plus the core tool definitions is about 800 to 900 tokens, which is close\nto or under that limit. Before this change, the facts happened to push the\nprefix over the minimum, so caching worked. If block 0 plus tools is under 1024\ntokens, the API will not cache it at all and every call will be a full-price\ninput. I could not check the real count offline.\n\nTo confirm after deploying: look at the first few entries in `usage.jsonl`.\nOrdinary messages should show `cache_read_input_tokens` near the size of block 0\nplus tools. If both `cache_creation_input_tokens` and `cache_read_input_tokens`\nstay at 0 for the static part, the prefix is under the minimum. The fix would then\nbe to add stable content to block 0 (for example, a longer profile section) until\nit crosses 1024 tokens. I did not pad the prompt with filler.\n\n## Not changed\n\n- Keyword-based tool selection (`select_tools`) still changes the tool list. A\n  message that matches a group such as \"plan\" or \"race\" changes the tools prefix,\n  which also misses the system cache. `NOTES.md` records that this filtering was a\n  deliberate win on tool tokens. Fixing that would mean sending all tools every\n  time, which trades cache hits for tool tokens, so I left it as is.\n- Nothing was committed, deployed or sent anywhere.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1280,"cache_read_input_tokens":37246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1280},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e29688-e74b-4241-a01a-4b7b8c9dd3e3","uuid":"e7a5026d-f4df-4eef-a3b2-1ec25c41ec64","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:12:35.733Z","req